<% content_for :title, "NuclearDirectoryBot · Nuclear Directory" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="description" content="NuclearDirectoryBot keeps Nuclear Directory up to date from public pages. It follows robots.txt, visits each page at most once a day and stops when blocked.">
<% end %>
<%= render "shared/site_header" %>

<main class="nd-page nd-page--narrow nd-prose">
  <h1 class="type-title-md">NuclearDirectoryBot</h1>
  <div class="nd-prose__intro">
    <p class="type-body-strong">NuclearDirectoryBot is the crawler that keeps Nuclear Directory up to date.</p>
    <p class="type-body">It reads public pages, such as regulator filings, company press releases and news reports, and looks for facts about the US nuclear industry.</p>
  </div>

  <section aria-labelledby="identity">
    <h2 id="identity" class="type-body-strong">It always says who it is</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Every request sends this user agent:</p>
    <pre class="nd-code type-data"><%= DataQuality::Fetcher::USER_AGENT %></pre>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="behaviour">
    <h2 id="behaviour" class="type-body-strong">It follows robots.txt and stops when blocked</h2>
    <p class="type-body">It fetches each page at most once a day and waits <%= DataQuality::Fetcher::HOST_INTERVAL %> seconds between requests to the same site.</p>
    <ul class="type-small text-ink-muted">
      <li>It checks every page against the site's robots.txt, including pages it's redirected to. It reads a site's robots.txt once per visit, not once per page.</li>
      <li>It asks only for changes (ETag and Last-Modified), so an unchanged page costs a short reply.</li>
      <li>When a site blocks it, it doesn't retry, work around the block or pretend to be a browser.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="blocking">
    <h2 id="blocking" class="type-body-strong">Block it with robots.txt</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Add these two lines. It stops on its next visit.</p>
    <pre class="nd-code type-data">User-agent: <%= DataQuality::Fetcher::AGENT_TOKEN %>
Disallow: /</pre>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact" class="type-body-strong">Questions about a visit</h2>
    <p class="type-body">Email <%= mail_to DirectoryHelper::CORRECTIONS_EMAIL, nil, class: "nd-link" %>.</p>
    <p class="type-small text-ink-muted">Include the time and the page, or the reference number from your firewall's block page, so we can find the request.</p>
  </section>
</main>
